    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **James Wood** (77.49) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91), who serve as our highest-upside plays. **James Wood** benefits from a favorable matchup against Ritchie and an elite .422 xwOBA, while **Tyler Soderstrom** draws a significant park factor boost (+10%) in what promises to be a high-efficiency environment. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) is a priority start; despite a tough opponent, he is capitalizing on a massive 14% boost from dynamic platoon splits and superior park conditions, making him essential despite the marginal risk of facing Lugo. **Brice Turang** (70.78) also provides a strong foundation, benefiting from the leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Ure\u00f1a, ensuring he remains a focal point for our SB-weighted strategy.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, with **Zach McKinstry** (49.14) serving as the most difficult omission. While he offers some utility, he was edged out by the superior plate appearance quality projected for our starters; the combination of a bottom-of-the-order assignment (-8%) and the need to preserve game caps kept him firmly on the pine. We are also closely monitoring the risks associated with **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll**, both of whom face Williams; his 2.99 xERA makes him an elite arm, resulting in an 18-19% penalty to their base scores. While **Corbin Carroll** is startable due to his leadoff upside and speed, we are cognizant that elite catcher pop times (-2.0%) could hamper his ability to accumulate steals tonight. We continue to hold **Vinnie Pasquantino** on the IL while awaiting updates, alongside stash assets like **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, and **Edwin Arroyo**, ensuring our roster flexibility is maintained for the final stretch.",
